 "text": "This glue was a failure. Now it's on desks everywhere. A 3M scientist, Spencer Silver, tries to make a super strong glue. He makes the opposite. A glue so weak it peels off and sticks again. Years later, his co-worker Art Fry is singing in his church choir. His bookmarks keep falling out of his hymn book. Then it clicks. What if the bookmark could stick? 3M tests the sticky pads as press and peel. It flops. But 3M doesn't quit. In 1978, they flood Boise, Idaho with free samples. People love them. Two years later, they hit stores across America as post-it notes. A failed glue turned desk icon. Every legend has a beginning.",
